{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1532320","formula":"C₁₁H₁₈N₂O₈","hill":"C11H18N2O8","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":18.0,"N":2.0,"O":8.0},"names":{"en":"Base J"},"descriptions":{"en":"β-D-Glucopyranosyloxymethyluracil or base J is a hypermodified nucleobase found in the DNA of kinetoplastids including the human pathogenic trypanosomes. It was discovered in 1993, in the trypanosome Trypanosoma brucei and was the first hypermodified nucleobase found in eukaryotic DNA; it has since been found in other kinetoplastids, including Leishmania. Within these organisms Base J acts as a RNA polymerase II transcription terminator, with its removal in knockout cells being accompanied by a massive read-through at RNA polymerase II termination sites, which ultimately proves lethal to the cell."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":129852278,"mass":304.25,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CNC(=O)N(C1=O)CO[C@H]2[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O2)CO)O)O)O","inchikey":"COFDJTNKDGKSGN-SVFDORGDSA-N","iupac":"3-[[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-1H-pyrimidine-2,4-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1532320","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base_J","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/129852278","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q181136","formula":"C₅H₉NO₄","names":{"en":"DL-glutamic acid","ru":"Глутаминовая кислота","uk":"Глутамінова кислота"},"elements":["H","C","N","O"],"fame":68,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q408032","formula":"C₁₀H₁₆N₂O₈","names":{"en":"Edetic acid","ru":"Этилендиаминтетрауксусная кислота","uk":"Етилендіамінтетраоцтова кислота"},"elements":["